  <prompt>Make the shared ADR-024 regarding builder usable for sprk_signal and sprk_decisionrecord, and move SignalWriter onto it, replacing its private "mirrors, does not copy" regarding code.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE BFF engineer. Expert in ADR-024 polymorphic regarding and the core-ancestor stamp.</role>
  <goal>One regarding builder serves To Do, Event, Signal and Decision Record; To Do and Event behaviour is byte-identical; Signal rows carry the Lookup pair type; the dedupe key no longer depends on reading the pair type column.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>D-133 (owner): writers use the shared regarding components, not mirrors. D-132 made Signal's pair type a Lookup (task 140). uac-r2 reviews the builder generalisation as its own commit.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Workspace/TodoRegardingBuilder.cs (ApplyResolverFieldsAsync, ApplyResolverPairAsync, RegardingLookupByEntity)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/Nodes/ActionCore/TaskActionCore.cs (existing reuse for sprk_event)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/SignalWriter.cs (~:236-245 doc, ~:695 dedupe key, ~:1202-1206 pair write)</file>
      <file>every reader of sprk_signal.sprk_regardingrecordtype as a string: grep src/server and src/solutions, src/client; known: SignalCoreRecordAccess.cs ~:115 ($select) and ToRow ~:1354 (from #1665), SignalWriter.cs ~:1206; full list in notes/140-schema-delta.md</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="uac-r2">Commit 1 (own commit, uac-r2 reviews in isolation): parameterise the builder by table (lookup map per table, untyped-pair tolerance). The existing TodoRegardingBuilder and TaskActionCore tests pass UNCHANGED; add one new test per table (sprk_signal, sprk_decisionrecord). Nothing else in that commit.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-133">Commit 2: SignalWriter uses the builder for the pair and the subject lookup; delete its private regarding code. A subject with no sprk_recordtype_ref row (communication, agreement) gets the id-only untyped shape and is never an error.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-132">The dedupe key keeps its value format {policy}|{subject logical name}|{subject id}[|episode], composed from the subject logical name the writer already holds, never read back from the pair type column. Existing keys on dev rows must still match after the change (test).</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">Update every reader that treated the Signal pair type as a string. Do not change ownership (143) or stamping registration (144). BFF hygiene: publish-size delta vs a fresh build of the docs branch base. Never use --no-verify or bare git stash; you cannot write .claude/.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Generalise the builder (commit 1) with tests; run TodoRegardingBuilder + TaskActionCore tests unchanged.</step>
    <step order="2">Move SignalWriter onto it (commit 2); update string readers; dedupe-key compatibility test.</step>
    <step order="3">Build, run Signal/Decision/Workspace unit tests and ArchTests; run the live SignalWriter seam test once on dev (env in current-task.md Q7 row) and verify zz- cleanup.</step>
    <step order="4">Mutation check: revert the untyped-pair tolerance and confirm its test fails.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">TodoRegardingBuilder and TaskActionCore tests pass without edits.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A Signal on a matter writes sprk_regardingmatter + sprk_regardingrecordid + sprk_regardingrecordtype as an EntityReference to the matter's sprk_recordtype_ref row.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A Signal on a communication (no sprk_recordtype_ref row) writes the id with no type and succeeds.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">At most one subject lookup is populated per row (ADR-024 invariant), on Signal and on the DR test table.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The dedupe key for an existing dev Signal is reproduced exactly by the new writer.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No code reads sprk_signal.sprk_regardingrecordtype as a string (grep evidence in the PR).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Schema-agreement guard (enforcement ladder; owner request 2026-10-12): a test reads the repo solution source `src/dataverse/solutions/SpaarkeMaster/Entities/sprk_Signal/Entity.xml` (and `sprk_DecisionRecord/Entity.xml`) for the declared type of `sprk_regardingrecordtype`, builds a Signal through the real SignalWriter build path, and asserts the written value's CLR shape matches the declared type (lookup → EntityReference to sprk_recordtype_ref; text → string). Must-fire control: the test fails if the writer emits a string while the XML declares a lookup (prove by mutation). Must-not-fire control: the correct writer passes. Record "Enforced by: <test name>" in notes/140-schema-delta.md.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">notes/140-schema-delta.md, CLAUDE.md §6 (pair-type gotcha) and the #1111 PR body are updated to say the hazard is closed by this task, naming the guard test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: the stated contract plus the cases named above; anything beyond needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

